From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:49:26 -0700
Subject: [Media] Require consistent resource length and don't retry SW
 failures

When a UrlData already has a known length from an earlier response,
reject subsequent 200 OK or 206 Partial Content responses (or
UrlData::MergeFrom merges) that report a different or unspecified
length. This prevents a service worker from splicing responses from two
different same-origin resources of different sizes onto the same
UrlData, which previously allowed leaking the second resource's length
either via DidFinishLoading()'s short-body retry Range header or by
overwriting UrlData::length() on a mid-resource 200 OK.

Additionally, do not retry failed loads in DidFail() when the response
was fetched via a service worker.

Fixed: 573265164
Change-Id: Ie02197b4c3f7c99d6b44e7147cfa67a44b9bf5ed
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8613828
Reviewed-by: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722390}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Picked as a prerequisite of a4a389ea3bf0 (UrlData::HasCompatibleLength()); it is
also the fix for crbug.com/573265164. DidFail(): this branch has no
IsRequestBlockedError / certificate-error early-return block, so only the
service-worker condition is added as its own block. Unit test changes were
not carried.

